# Git Conventions
- Commit format: `type(scope): description` — e.g. `feat(hero): add parallax layer`, `fix(nav): mobile menu focus trap`.
- Types: `feat`, `fix`, `refactor`, `style`, `docs`, `chore`.
- One branch per task in `tasks.md` (generated by Cursor per `portfolio-spec.md`'s first-session instructions). Do feature work on the branch, not directly on `main`.
- Commit at logical checkpoints within a task (e.g. structure → content wired → motion applied), not one giant commit per task.
- Merge finished branches into `main` with `--no-ff` (`git merge --no-ff <branch>`) so the graph keeps an explicit merge commit.
